title: Sarie Marais
artist: Septimus Winner / J. P. Toerien
origin: South Africa
culture: South African
genre: Folk
language: af
key: G major
tempo: 108
meter: 4/4
pickup: 1
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: march
guide: clarinet
year: 1900
attribution: Afrikaans song from the time of the Anglo-Boer wars (about 1889 to 1900); the words are usually credited to Jacobus Petrus Toerien (died 1920) and the tune is Septimus Winner's "Ellie Rhee" of 1865 (Winner died in 1902), so both are public domain. Verse 1 and chorus, melody as printed in the F.A.K.-Volksangbundel.
source_url: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volk_en_Vaderland_54_-_Sarie_Marais.png
tags: south africa, afrikaans, march, folk, love, homesick

